team":"TEN","distance":0.6236,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"NE","distance":0.6973,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"TEN","distance":0.6996,"shared":12,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"SF","distance":0.1333,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"JAX","distance":0.309,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Anthony Campanile"},{"season":2023,"team":"CHI","distance":0.3237,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"NO","distance":0.3347,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennis Allen"},{"season":2023,"team":"PHI","distance":0.339,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Falcons are 3-7 through week 10 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 258 to 201. The offense ranks 27th in EPA per play and the defense 20th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. What sets them apart is the 3rd highest screen rate in the league.","offense":"The Falcons offense has been well below average by EPA per play so far, and it has been much better running the ball than passing it. They have been one of the most run-heavy teams in the league, passing less often than game situations would predict. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 3rd highest screen rate in the league. Michael Penix Jr. has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Drake London, who has drawn 28% of the targets.","defense":"The Falcons defense has been a little below average by EPA allowed per play so far. Za'Darius Smith has led the way with 4.5 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 7th lowest in the league.","special":"The Falcons have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 75% of field goals, which is well below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the offensive line, about 29% of the money on the books. Their offensive line was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Michael Penix Jr. has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,730 yards. Drake London has been the clear top target with 28% of the looks and 801 receiving yards. Bijan Robinson has handled most of the work in the backfield with 74% of the carries. On defense, Za'Darius Smith leads the team with 4.5 sacks.","coaching":"Kevin Stefanski is calling the offense as head coach and Jeff Ulbrich is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Panthers and the 2023 Broncos under Sean Payton. Their defense looks most like the 2023 49ers and the 2025 Jaguars under Anthony Campanile.","trends":"The offense went from 24th in EPA per play in 2025 to 27th so far this season, a modest decline. The defense moved from 15th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 20th so far this season, a modest decline. The biggest change in approach was blitz rate, which went from 35% to 26%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}